{"name":"Graceful Garden","hex":"#cba9d0","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"graceful","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having or showing grace in movement, shape, or proportion.","Magnanimous, lacking arrogance or complaint; gracious."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graceful"},{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/500px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/1280px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wi